// `then CHECK:(value)`, after a case's expected values and before its
// constraints, as many as the case needs: a function the case's process calls
// once the call under test has returned, and the value it must return. Each is
// a "then" node in `thennode` -- the check's name in s1, its value in nl1, and
// the index of the case it is written on in i1.
//
// `then` also begins three other clauses -- `prints`, `eprints` and `calls`
// (docs/TESTS.md) -- told apart by the keyword after it; more/dispatch.id
// routes to whichever this one is.

case_rest(int[] pos) {
  case_thens(pos);
  if(cur_text(pos) == "[") {
    advance(pos);
    cons_list(pos);
    advance(pos);
  }
} return void;
